Software Requirements Specification (SRS)

 ## Turf — Booking & Discovery Platform

 **Version:** 1.2\
 **Target Market:** Nairobi, Kenya\
 **Application Type:** Mobile-first responsive web application\
 **Future Module:** 3D Turf Map & Navigation

 > **v1.2 change:** Online payment (M-Pesa) is deferred from the MVP. Players currently pay at the venue after playing, and requiring upfront payment would hinder adoption. The MVP focuses on turf management: bookings are reserved through Turf and paid at the venue, where staff record the payment. Online payment remains a future module (§12). See `docs/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md`.

---

 # 1\. Introduction

 ## 1.1 Purpose

 Turf is a web-based platform for discovering, booking, and managing football turfs in Nairobi.

 The system will allow customers to search for turfs, view availability, reserve time slots, and manage their bookings. Payment is made at the venue in the MVP.

 Turf owners will be able to manage venues, pitches, availability, pricing, staff, bookings (including walk-ins), payments received, and revenue through an owner dashboard.

 Administrators will manage users, venues, bookings, payments, disputes, and platform operations.

 A future version of Turf will introduce an interactive **3D Turf Map & Navigation subsystem**, allowing users to explore football venues through a simplified 3D representation of roads, turfs, entrances, landmarks, and navigation routes.

---

 # 2\. Product Vision

 Turf aims to become a digital platform for discovering and accessing football facilities.

 The initial product focuses on:

 > **Find → Check availability → Book → Play → Pay at venue**

 The long-term vision expands this into:

 > **Discover → Explore → Navigate → Book → Play**

 The 3D map is therefore considered a future differentiation layer rather than a dependency of the core booking system.

