 # 11\. Booking Management

 Customers shall be able to:

 1. Select a venue.
2. Select a turf.
3. Select a date.
4. Select a time.
5. Review booking information (price payable at the venue).
6. Submit the booking.
7. Receive confirmation (immediately, or after owner approval where the venue requires it).

 Venue staff shall also be able to create bookings directly from the owner calendar for walk-in, phone and WhatsApp customers, without the customer having an account.

 The system shall prevent overlapping bookings, including between staff-created and customer-created bookings.

 ## 11.1 Booking States

```
PENDING      awaiting owner approval
CONFIRMED
REJECTED
CANCELLED
COMPLETED
NO_SHOW
```

 Payment status is tracked separately from booking status:

```
UNPAID
PARTIALLY_PAID
PAID
WAIVED
```

 ## 11.2 Temporary Holds (deferred)

 Temporary holds (`HELD`, `PAYMENT_PENDING`, `EXPIRED`) and refund states (`REFUND_PENDING`, `REFUNDED`) are only needed for online payment and are deferred with it (§12).

 The database shall enforce booking integrity to prevent concurrent customers or staff from successfully reserving the same inventory.

