 # 12\. Payment System

 ## 12.1 MVP — Payment at the Venue

 Customers pay at the venue, as they do today. The system shall:

 - Show the price payable at the venue when booking.
- Allow staff to record payments against a booking (amount, method: cash / M-Pesa / other, optional M-Pesa transaction code).
- Allow partial payments and waivers.
- Allow staff to void a recorded payment with a reason (audit-logged).
- Track payment status per booking.
- Report revenue and outstanding unpaid amounts.

 ## 12.2 Future — Online Payment

 Online payment (M-Pesa STK Push) is deferred. When introduced it shall:

 - Initiate payment requests.
- Associate payments with bookings.
- Receive and verify payment callbacks.
- Handle duplicate callbacks safely.
- Store transaction references.
- Handle failed transactions.
- Support deposits and refunds.

 The payment architecture should be provider-independent, and online payments shall be recorded in the same payment records as venue payments so that bookings and reporting are unaffected.

